# ============================================================
#  MAIN CHAIN: The Hollow Star (v2, docs/plots/hollowstar-v2.md)
#
#  Something sleeps beneath the lake, sealed by Lumenhold's founders. Kael Dumont's family serve it. The wiring is in
#  content/events/hollowstar/threads.grim: four acts, each a story thread whose climax raises the arc's clock to the
#  next act's opener (the arc's beats are deadlines), and the Night, a scene in one sitting. The acts' openers and
#  confrontations are in chain_hollowstar_acts.grim, the newer cards in content/events/hollowstar/.
#  Here: Act I's finds (the dream, the ledger, the bell) and its climax (hs_grey_stranger); Kael's secret and the man
#  in grey's offers (Act II); the seventh tower and its key (Act III); the headmistress's summons (Act IV); and the
#  Night's tunnel, wall and door with their aftermaths.
#  Alignment (Lumen + / Hollow -) is the moral axis: the Star's gifts pull toward the Hollow; refusing them, toward the
#  Lumen. Outcomes fill the yearbook's mystery line: sealed / bargained / freed / failed / fled / held the line /
#  claimed (game over) / bystander.
# ============================================================

@event hs_dreams_begin
time: morning
title: The Black Star Dream
class: story
tone: eerie
when: turn >= 5 and not has(hollow_dreams)
weight: 14
art: moon
tags: mystery hollowstar
thread: hs_omens
scene: A dreamscape: a frozen lake seen from beneath, a round door glowing at the bottom, and above it a star that is a hole in the sky.
text: You dream of the lake from underneath. There is a round door at the bottom, and above the water a star that is not a light but an absence. A voice says your name like it is tasting it. You wake with frost on your pillow.
> left: Write the dream down
  lore +small
  find lead_black_star_dream
  gain hollow_dreams
  hs_omens_progress
  say: Your notes fill four pages. In the morning you don't remember writing the last line: "It is not asleep. It is waiting."
> right: Ask Seraphine what it means
  meet seraphine
  rel seraphine +small
  find lead_black_star_dream
  gain hollow_dreams
  hs_omens_progress
  say: Seraphine listens, then hands you a sprig of lavender. "It won't stop the dreams," she says. "But it'll make them smell nicer."

@event hs_grey_stranger
title: A Man in Grey
arc: hollowstar
beat: 2
slot: night
class: story
tone: tense
when: met(kael)
art: snow
tags: mystery hollowstar danger
thread: hs_omens
# Act I's climax (v2): two of the act's finds bring it early (hs_omens_progress), the deadline otherwise; it opens Act II.
scene: A frozen fountain in a moonlit courtyard; a tall man in a grey coat facing a pale young man who is shouting, frost spreading from both.
on_show:
  advance hollowstar to 4
text: The courtyard fountain freezes mid-splash with a crack like a whip. Kael, who never raises his voice, is shouting at a tall man in a grey coat: "Tell her no. I did." The man smiles. "The door under the lake will be opened, by you or by your sister. Your mother doesn't mind which." Then he turns his head and says your name, which nobody told him.
> left: Back into the shadows
  guile +tiny
  mood -tiny
  find lead_man_in_grey
  say: You back away. He looks at the exact spot where you're hiding, smiles, and walks out through the gate with frost blooming in his footprints. You don't sleep. Neither, you suspect, does Kael.
> right: Step out beside Kael
  hint: He'll remember your face.
  rel kael +large
  health -tiny
  find lead_man_in_grey
  flag confronted_grey
  say: "He said no." It comes out louder than you meant. The man in grey studies you, inclines his head and leaves; the cold he leaves behind bites through your sleeves. Kael's hands are shaking. "You shouldn't have done that," he says. "...Thank you."

@event hs_founders_records
title: The Founders' Ledger
place: library
time: morning afternoon
class: story
tone: eerie
when: clue(lead_founders_archive) and not clue(founders_ledger)
weight: 14
art: book
tags: mystery hollowstar study
thread: hs_omens
scene: A dusty archive vault, a giant ledger open on a lectern, one page carefully razored out.
text: In the archive vault you find the Founders' Ledger, three hundred years old. The entry for the academy's founding year has been cut out with a razor. But the page beneath still holds the impression of the pen.
> left: Leave it — this feels dangerous
  mood +tiny
  say: You close the ledger. The dust settles. Some doors are better left alone. Probably.
> right: Rub charcoal over the page
  challenge research apprentice+:
    win:
      flag knows_founders_seal
      find knows_founders_seal
      find founders_ledger
      lore +small
      hs_omens_progress
      say: Ghostly letters emerge: "Seven towers, seven locks. The Star sleeps beneath the water. The key is a star that holds no light." The founders built the academy as a seal.
    lose:
      lore +tiny
      say: The impression is too faint. You make out only three words: "...beneath the water..."

@event hs_restricted_founders
title: The Chained Drafts
place: restricted_section
time: midnight
class: story
tone: eerie
when: clue(lead_founders_archive) and not clue(founders_ledger)
weight: 16
art: lock
tags: mystery hollowstar study
thread: hs_omens
scene: A dark aisle of the Restricted Section at midnight, a bundle of yellowed drafts chained to a shelf, the chain faintly glowing.
text: The archive's ledger has its founding page cut out. The Restricted Section keeps the founders' own drafts, chained to a shelf at the very back, and the chain is warm to the touch. Somewhere behind you, a book turns its own page.
> left: Work the chain loose
  challenge deceive journeyman:
    win:
      flag knows_founders_seal
      find founders_ledger
      find knows_founders_seal
      health -tiny
      hs_omens_progress
      say: The links give one by one, and burn your fingers doing it. The drafts say it plainly, in three hands: "Seven towers, seven locks. The Star sleeps beneath the water. The key is a star that holds no light." Lumenhold is a seal.
    lose:
      gain detention
      mood -small
      say: The chain shrieks like a ward. You're out of the window before the prefect arrives, but not before he sees your face. Detention, and a long look from the librarian.
> right: Copy the shelf-list instead
  lore +small
  mana -tiny
  find lead_seventh_tower
  say: The drafts' shelf-list is less guarded and nearly as strange. One entry reads only "Key: the seventh tower, top room. Do not lend." You copy it out by the light of a reading charm you have to keep alive for an hour, and it leaves you drained.

@event hs_boathouse_bell
title: The Hatch in the Boathouse
place: boathouse
time: evening night midnight
class: story
tone: eerie
when: clue(lead_lake_breathed) and not clue(lake_bell)
weight: 16
art: bell
tags: mystery hollowstar
thread: hs_omens
scene: The inside of an old wooden boathouse at night, a square hatch open in the floorboards, stone steps leading down into dark water.
text: Under a coil of rotten rope in the boathouse there's a hatch, and under the hatch, stone steps going down into the lake. The air coming up smells of cold bronze. From somewhere below, very faint, a bell is tolling under the water.
> left: Go down the steps
  challenge feat apprentice:
    win:
      flag found_lake_tunnel
      find lake_bell
      health -tiny
      hs_omens_progress
      say: The steps become a tunnel under the lakebed, dry and ice-cold, running toward the sound. You follow it until you can see the bell's green rim in the dark ahead. Then you turn back, frozen to the bone, and remember every turning.
    lose:
      find lake_bell
      health -small
      hs_omens_progress
      say: The third step is ice. You go into the water to the chest and come up gasping, but you've seen it: a tunnel under the lake, running toward the bell. You walk home soaked.
> right: Listen at the waterline
  find lake_bell
  mood -small
  hs_omens_progress
  say: You lie on the boards with your ear to the gap. The bell tolls seven times, slow, and between the strokes you hear a draught moving under the lake, the way air moves in a corridor. Something down there is a door. You don't sleep well.

@event hs_seraphine_shadow
title: One Star Too Many
place: observatory
slot: evening
class: story
tone: eerie
actor: seraphine
when: met(seraphine) and not clue(second_shadow) and (clue(lead_black_star_dream) or seen(hs_shadow_late) > 0)
weight: 16
art: star
tags: mystery hollowstar
thread: hs_escalation
scene: An observatory at night, the great telescope tilted down toward the window and the lake below, a seer pointing at the reflection of the stars in the water.
text: Seraphine has turned the great telescope down, not at the sky but at the lake, where the stars are reflected. "Look," she says. "In the water. There's one star too many, and it's dark." She counts under her breath. "It wasn't there in my dream. It was in yours."
> left: Chart it with her
  meet seraphine
  find second_shadow
  lore +small
  hs_escalation_progress
  health -tiny
  say: You chart it till dawn on the cold floor: a small dark shape in the reflection that has no star above it, sitting exactly over the middle of the lake. Your knees never quite forgive you.
> right: Tell her about your dream
  meet seraphine
  find second_shadow
  rel seraphine +medium
  hs_escalation_progress
  mood -small
  say: She finishes your sentences, three of them, before you've started them. Then she shows you the dark star in the water, right over the middle of the lake. You both stop talking for a long time.

@event hs_kael_truth
title: What Kael Is Running From
class: story
tone: tense
when: (clue(lead_man_in_grey) or clues(hollowstar) >= 1) and rel(kael) >= 15 and not flag(kael_told)
actor: kael
weight: 16
art: snow
tags: mystery hollowstar social
thread: hs_investigation
# v2: a confrontation on the page; you corner him, and it comes out shouted.
scene: Two students on an observatory roof at night, one shouting with frost racing out from his boots across the leads, the other standing their ground.
text: It comes to a head on the observatory roof. You've had a year of his silences and you tell him so, loudly. He shouts back, for the first time ever: "My family serve the thing under this lake! They sent me here to open its door!" Frost races out from his boots across the roof. Then, quieter: "I came to stop them. Some nights I'm not sure which I'll do."
> left: "Then we stop them together."
  flag kael_told kael_ally
  rel kael +large
  spark kael +tiny
  alignment +small
  find kael_family
  hs_investigation_progress
  if bond(kael) == "none":
    bond kael friend
  say: He looks at you for a long moment, and the frost on the roof melts a little. "Together," he repeats, as if trying out a word from another language.
> right: Tell the headmistress
  flag kael_told reported_kael
  rel kael -huge
  rel isolde +medium
  alignment +tiny
  find kael_family
  hs_investigation_progress
  say: The headmistress thanks you gravely. The next day Kael is moved to a room in the headmistress's tower. He doesn't look at you anymore.

@event hs_star_mark
title: The Cold Coin Burns
class: story
tone: eerie
when: (flag(star_coin) or flag(bell_fragment)) and not has(star_mark) and not flag(threw_star)
weight: 12
art: star
tags: mystery hollowstar magic
thread: hollowstar
scene: A student's open palm, a pale star-shaped mark glowing on it, a blackened coin smoking on the floor beside them.
text: The black-starred relic you've been carrying burns suddenly, so cold it feels hot. When you drop it, there's a pale star-shaped mark on your palm. It hums when you're near the lake.
> left: Throw the relic into the lake
  flag threw_star
  unflag star_coin bell_fragment
  alignment +medium
  mood +tiny
  say: It sinks without a ripple. The mark on your hand fades — almost entirely. Something under the water sighs.
> right: Keep it. Feel the power.
  gain star_mark
  arcana +medium
  alignment -medium
  say: The mark pulses with every heartbeat. Spells come easier now. Much easier. That should probably worry you more than it does.

@event hs_grey_offer
title: An Offer in Grey
class: story
tone: eerie
when: turn >= 18 and (clues(hollowstar) >= 2 or alignment <= -30) and not flag(grey_offer_seen)
weight: 12
art: mask
tags: mystery hollowstar danger
thread: hs_investigation
scene: A grey-coated man sitting uninvited at a library table, a black velvet box open in front of him, every candle around him burning blue.
text: Every candle in the room goes blue at once. The man in grey is sitting at your table, uninvited, a black velvet box open in front of him. "You've been asking about the Star," he says. "It has started asking about you. It could make you extraordinary. All it wants is a door opened." He turns the box toward you. Inside it you see yourself, burning.
> left: "Get out."
  hint: He leaves. He remembers.
  alignment +small
  flag grey_offer_seen
  mood +tiny
  gain grey_watching
  queue hs_grey_return within 2..4
  hs_investigation_progress
  say: He inclines his head and leaves. The candles go back to yellow. You realise your hands are trembling, and that he looked at you on the way out the way a man looks at a lock.
> right: "...What would it give me?"
  hint: Everything, a little. The nights turn cold.
  flag grey_offer_seen hollow_tempted
  arcana +small
  lore +small
  alchemy +small
  charm +small
  vigor +small
  guile +small
  alignment -medium
  gain star_taste
  queue hs_grey_return within 2..4
  hs_investigation_progress
  say: He shows you, just for a moment. Power, endless and cold, in everything you can do at once. When he's gone you can still taste it, and that night you dream of water closing over your head.

@event hs_grey_return
title: A Small Service
trigger: queued
defer: off_campus
class: story
tone: eerie
art: mask
tags: mystery hollowstar danger
thread: hs_investigation
# hs_grey_offer's follow-up (feedback 2026-10-16): the man in grey comes back with a first, small ask.
scene: A grey-coated man on a frozen garden bench, a sealed letter held out between two gloved fingers, the fountain beside him iced over.
text: {flag(hollow_tempted): The man in grey is on a bench in the winter garden, and the fountain beside him has frozen mid-splash. "You liked what you tasted," he says. "Here is how it continues." He holds out a sealed letter. "Leave this under the third plank of the boathouse jetty. Nothing more."|The man in grey is on a bench in the winter garden, and the fountain beside him has frozen mid-splash. "You told me to get out," he says, pleasantly. "I did. Now a small thing, and I'll stay out." He holds out a sealed letter. "The third plank of the boathouse jetty. Nothing more."}
> left: Take the letter to the jetty
  hint: Hollow. He pays in what he promised.
  alignment -small
  flag hollow_tempted grey_errand
  gold +medium
  gain star_taste
  say: You do it at midnight, with the lake breathing under the planks. In the morning there's a purse on your pillow and the cold dreams are back, sweeter than before.
> right: Drop it in the fountain unread
  hint: Lumen. He won't thank you.
  alignment +small
  mood -small
  lose star_taste
  gain grey_watching
  say: You break the ice and push the letter under. The ink runs blue. He watches it sink, then you, and then he isn't there, and the fountain starts to splash again as if nothing had happened.

@event hs_grey_invitation
time: evening night
title: A Seat at the Northern Table
class: story
tone: eerie
when: alignment <= -60 and turn >= 12 and not flag(hollow_courted)
weight: 16
art: letter
tags: mystery hollowstar danger
thread: hollowstar
scene: A black-edged letter on a dormitory pillow, its wax seal pressed with a star that has no light in it.
text: There is a letter on your pillow, sealed with a black star. The handwriting is beautiful. "The families have watched you with great interest," it says. "There is a seat for you at our table, when the door is opened. Come to the boathouse at midnight, or burn this. Either is an answer."
> left: Go to the boathouse
  flag hollow_courted hollow_tempted
  alignment -small
  guile +small
  health -small
  say: The man in grey is waiting with two cups of something hot. He talks to you as an equal for an hour. You come back with frost in your hair and the feeling of having been measured, and found to fit.
> right: Burn it
  alignment +medium
  mood -small
  say: The paper burns blue and slow, and smells of the lake. It takes a long time to go out. Climbing back from where you've been is slower still, but this is a step.

@event hs_grey_tests
title: The Good Argument
class: story
tone: eerie
when: alignment >= 30 and turn >= 14 and not flag(grey_tested)
weight: 12
art: mask
tags: mystery hollowstar danger
thread: hollowstar
scene: A grey-coated man standing beside a student at the infirmary window, both looking down at a first-year with a bandaged arm.
text: The man in grey falls into step beside you outside the infirmary. "You help people," he says pleasantly. "I admire it. But think how many more you could help with real power. The Star doesn't care what it's used for. Only that someone uses it."
> left: "No."
  flag grey_tested
  alignment +small
  mood -tiny
  say: "No," you say. He smiles as if you'd said something charming, and leaves. The first-year in the window waves at you. You wave back, and your hand is shaking.
> right: "...How many more?"
  flag grey_tested hollow_tempted
  alignment -medium
  lore +small
  say: He tells you. The numbers are very large and very cold. That night, you dream of the lake from underneath, and you are not frightened in the dream.

@event hs_wardens_notice
title: The Headmistress Takes Note
class: story
tone: warm
actor: isolde
when: alignment >= 60 and turn >= 12 and not flag(wardens_noticed)
weight: 16
art: crown
tags: mystery hollowstar
thread: hollowstar
scene: A tall woman in dark robes pausing on a stair to look down at one student among many, a silver ring glinting on her hand.
text: On the grand stair the headmistress stops beside you. "Several people have told me about you," she says, "and not one of them was complaining. That is rare." Her silver ring catches the light. "I keep a list of students I would trust with a door. Don't let it go to your head."
> left: "I'd be honoured."
  meet isolde
  flag wardens_noticed
  rel isolde +medium
  mood -tiny
  say: "Good," she says. "Honour is a heavy thing to carry. Practise." She walks on. You stand on the stair for some time.
> right: "What kind of door?"
  meet isolde
  flag wardens_noticed
  rel isolde +small
  lore +small
  say: Her short, delighted laugh. "The kind that ought to stay shut," she says. "Keep asking questions like that. Just not on the stairs."

@event hs_seventh_tower
title: The Seventh Tower
place: seventh_tower
slot: evening
class: story
tone: eerie
when: clue(lead_seventh_tower) and not flag(star_key) and not flag(gave_star_key) and not flag(key_taken)
weight: 16
art: tower
tags: mystery hollowstar
thread: hs_escalation
scene: The top of a narrow, abandoned tower, cobwebbed and moonlit, with a wall bearing a star-shaped recess.
text: The seventh tower has been locked for a century, and its wards start shrieking the moment you touch the door. You go up anyway, two steps at a time, while lights come on all over the academy. At the very top, a single room: dust, moonlight, and a star-shaped hollow in the wall, holding something that does not reflect any light.
> left: Take it quietly
  challenge deceive journeyman:
    win:
      flag star_key
      find star_key
      mood -small
      hs_escalation_progress
      queue hs_key_breakfast in 1
      say: A key shaped like a star, black as a hole in the world. As you lift it, every candle in the academy goes out for one breath. You walk back in the dark with it cold against your ribs, and you don't sleep.
    lose:
      gain detention
      mood -small
      say: A ward shrieks. A prefect finds you on the stairs. You get detention and a very long look from the headmistress.
> right: Take it boldly
  challenge spell journeyman:
    win:
      flag star_key
      find star_key
      mana -small
      hs_escalation_progress
      queue hs_key_breakfast in 1
      say: You tear through the ward with brute force, and it drains you to the bone. The key comes free. Every candle in the academy goes out for one breath, and somewhere below, a door hears it.
    lose:
      health -large
      say: The ward throws you down two flights of stairs.

@event hs_key_breakfast
title: Something of Mine
class: story
tone: tense
trigger: queued
defer: off_campus
actor: isolde
art: key
tags: mystery hollowstar
thread: hollowstar
scene: The high table at breakfast, the headmistress setting down her cup and looking along the hall at one student, the candles behind her newly lit.
text: At breakfast the headmistress sets down her cup and looks straight at you along the whole length of the hall. Afterwards she is waiting at the door. "Every candle in my academy went out," she says pleasantly, "and you have something of mine."
> left: Give her the key
  meet isolde
  unflag star_key
  flag gave_star_key wardens_noticed
  rel isolde +medium
  alignment +small
  say: She takes it in a gloved hand without looking at it. "Thank you. It will be where it is needed, on the night. So, I hope, will you." You feel lighter, and a little robbed.
> right: Keep it
  meet isolde
  flag kept_star_key
  rel isolde -medium
  say: A long pause. "Then keep it close," she says, "and never let it near the water before its time. People will come asking for it. Not all of them will ask." From then on, the man in grey always seems to know where you are.

@event hs_isolde_summons
title: The Headmistress Knows
class: story
tone: eerie
trigger: auto
when: final_year and month <= 8 and not flag(hs_early) and (clues(hollowstar) >= 3 or flag(kael_ally) or flag(wardens_noticed) or flag(sided_wardens) or flag(sided_dumonts) or flag(sided_self))
priority: 45
actor: isolde
art: crown
tags: mystery hollowstar story
thread: hs_convergence
# v2: no longer pinned to months 3-7; it waits on Act IV. If the man in grey took the key, the Wardens fetch it back
# here (one of the ways back that isn't a fight, decision 2026-10-26).
scene: A circular study at the top of a tower, walls lined with sleeping portraits, the headmistress standing by a window over the lake, Thorne and Maud beside her, a black-sealed letter on the desk.
text: The headmistress summons you to her tower. Thorne is there, and Maud, and on the desk between them is a letter with a black-star seal, opened. "The Dumonts' mother is coming south for the Blossom moon," Isolde says. "She means to open the door herself. I need people I trust beneath the lake. Or you may walk away, and no one in this room will blame you."
> left: Walk away
  meet isolde
  flag hollow_out
  mood +small
  say: "Wise," she says, and you can't tell if she means it. Maud looks at her tea. "Then stay above," says the headmistress, "and keep the first-years indoors."
> right: "I'll be there."
  alignment +small
  meet isolde
  flag warden_trial
  find star_key
  rel isolde +large
  arcana +small
  mood -small
  say: She presses a silver ward-ring into your hand. "{flag(star_key): The founders' key is with you. Keep it close.|{flag(gave_star_key) or flag(key_taken): The founders' key is in my desk; the Wardens saw to that.|The founders' key is kept at the top of the seventh tower.}} On the night, it comes down with us. Learn quickly. You have until Blossomtide."
  if not flag(star_key):
    unflag key_taken
    flag gave_star_key

@event hs_the_night
title: The Night the Lake Froze
class: story
tone: eerie
trigger: auto
when: final_year and clock(hollowstar) >= 12 and hs_called()
priority: 70
art: snow
tags: mystery hollowstar danger
thread: hs_night
# The Night's entry (v2) at the deadline (the clock reaches 12 at y4m9); hs_go_down_early starts the Night at its
# second card instead, having frozen the lake itself.
scene: The whole lake frozen white in the middle of spring, cracks glowing from beneath, a ring of lanterns out on the ice, students crowding the towers' windows.
text: In the middle of spring, the lake freezes in a single breath, from shore to shore. Cracks glow beneath the ice. Every candle in the academy leans toward the water. Out on the ice, lanterns are moving in a ring: someone is already there. Under it all the bell is tolling, {clue(lake_bell): the note you followed once|a note you've never heard and somehow know}.
> left: Go down beneath the lake
  find lake_bell
  queue hs_night_company now
  say: You run for the boathouse. Behind you, someone is shouting your name. You don't stop.
> right: Stay above and protect the students
  close hollowstar
  alignment +small
  health -medium
  renown +large
  rel isolde +small
  flag hollow_held_line
  say: You hold the doors of the first-year tower all night against things made of frost and whispers. By dawn the lake thaws. Something below is still asleep, for now, and forty children are alive who might not have been.

@event hs_tunnel
title: The Man in the Tunnel
class: story
tone: tense
trigger: queued
type: menu
priority: 95
art: mask
tags: mystery hollowstar danger
thread: hs_night
# v2: whoever came down with you rides along (`with npc`: Kael's or Ilse's Hoarfrost in the fight). The talk pays off
# ilse_truth and kael_family; slipping past, lake_bell. Then Ilse (if she was taken), then your shadow.
scene: A slick stone tunnel under the ice, lit blue from above, a tall man in a grey coat standing in the middle of it with his hands folded.
text: The tunnel runs down under the ice, slick and glowing blue. Halfway down, the man in grey is waiting, alone, as if he has all night. {flag(night_kael): "Kael. Your mother is disappointed." "She always is," says Kael, and the walls frost over.|{flag(night_ilse): "Ilse. You were meant to open it." "I know what I was meant for," she says.|{flag(night_isolde): "Headmistress. You're late by sixty years." "Then I'll be thorough," she says.|"Go back up," he says pleasantly. "This isn't your door."}}}
> fight: Break through him
  hint: Combat. Whoever came down with you fights beside you.
  if flag(ilse_taken) and not flag(ilse_went_north):
    queue hs_night_ilse now with npc
  else:
    queue hs_night_shadow now with npc
  challenge combat master- unlikely with npc:
    win:
      flag hs_tunnel_clear
      say: You hit him {flag(night_kael): with Kael's frost at the same moment|square}, and he slides back along the ice, {flag(grey_beaten): and this time he isn't surprised; he's angry|surprised for the first time in four years}. He bows, and is simply not there any more. The road down is clear.
    lose:
      night_hurt += 1
      say: He takes your last spell on his own gloved hand and closes his fist on it, then steps back to let you pass, smiling. "Go on, then. She's waiting." You go down bruised, and late.
> talk: Talk your way past
  hint: Charm. What the Dumonts were raised for is your best argument.
  if flag(ilse_taken) and not flag(ilse_went_north):
    queue hs_night_ilse now with npc
  else:
    queue hs_night_shadow now with npc
  challenge negotiate master- unlikely +1 if clue(ilse_truth) +1 if flag(ilse_saved) +1 if flag(mother_answered):
    win:
      flag hs_tunnel_clear
      find ilse_truth
      find kael_family
      say: You tell him {flag(ilse_taken): that Kael has chosen, and Ilse will|that the Dumont children have chosen, both of them}, and that you know exactly what they were raised for and what it cost them. For a moment he looks old. Then he steps aside. It costs you something, seeing that look.
    lose:
      night_hurt += 1
      find ilse_truth
      find kael_family
      say: He listens courteously, then tells you, kindly, everything the Dumonts did to their children and why. It takes a long time. He lets you pass only once you've heard every word. You arrive shaken, and late.
> slip: Find another way down
  hint: Guile. Easier if you know the old tunnels, or the bell's note.
  if flag(ilse_taken) and not flag(ilse_went_north):
    queue hs_night_ilse now with npc
  else:
    queue hs_night_shadow now with npc
  challenge deceive master- unlikely +1 if flag(found_lake_tunnel) +1 if clue(lake_bell):
    win:
      flag hs_tunnel_clear
      say: You follow the bell's note into a side passage he doesn't know, the one its rope once ran through. You come out below him, breathless, and he never sees you go.
    lose:
      night_hurt += 1
      say: The side passage is half flooded. You come out soaked and freezing below him, and late, and he calls a polite good evening after you down the tunnel.

@event hs_threshold
title: The Founders' Words
class: story
tone: eerie
trigger: queued
type: menu
priority: 95
art: book
tags: mystery hollowstar danger
thread: hs_night
# v2: every clue about the seal opens a lock here (seven_locks, the ledger, the founders' seal, Edmund's wand), and the
# wall pays them off for anyone who never found them.
scene: A wall of black stone at the end of a tunnel, carved with lines of script that drift when not looked at, seven round locks set in it, a faint bell-tone hanging in the air.
text: The tunnel ends at a wall of black stone, carved with the founders' words in a script that drifts when you look away, and set with seven round locks, one for each tower. {chosen(hs_maud_locks, right): You know them. Maud told you.|{clue(seven_locks): You know them.|You count them twice.}} Behind it the bell is tolling. {flag(night_maud): Maud lays a hand on the stone and says, "Hello again."|}
> read: Read the founders' words
  hint: Lore. Everything you learned about the seal makes it easier.
  queue hs_beneath now with npc
  challenge research master- unlikely +1 if clue(knows_founders_seal) +1 if clue(seven_locks) +1 if clue(founders_ledger) +1 if flag(winter_isolde) +1 if flag(night_isolde):
    win:
      say: {clue(knows_founders_seal): You've read these words before, in pieces.|You've never read them, but they read themselves to you, line by line.} Said whole, they turn the seven locks one after another, and the wall opens like a door. "Seven towers, seven locks," you hear yourself say. "The key is a star that holds no light."
      flag hs_threshold_read
      find seven_locks
      find knows_founders_seal
    lose:
      night_hurt += 1
      find seven_locks
      find knows_founders_seal
      say: You stumble on the last line, and only six of the locks turn. The wall opens a crack. You squeeze through it, and it takes skin off your shoulder on the way, and the words follow you down the dark like a rhyme.
> force: Force the locks
  hint: Arcana, and it hurts. Maud's wards and Edmund's wand help.
  queue hs_beneath now with npc
  challenge spell master- unlikely +1 if flag(winter_maud) +1 if has_item(edmunds_silver_wand) +1 if flag(night_maud):
    win:
      flag hs_threshold_read
      find seven_locks
      find knows_founders_seal
      say: {has_item(edmunds_silver_wand): Edmund's wand hums the bell's note against the stone, and the locks turn to it one by one.|You trace the old wards backwards into the stone, {flag(winter_maud): the way Maud showed you|the way the stone seems to want}, and the locks turn one by one.} The wall cracks down the middle and opens. Your hands ache to the elbow.
    lose:
      night_hurt += 1
      find seven_locks
      find knows_founders_seal
      say: The stone fights back. Six locks give; the seventh you break, and it breaks something in your hands too. You get through in the end, raw and shaking.

@event hs_beneath
title: The Door Beneath the Lake
class: story
tone: eerie
trigger: queued
type: menu
priority: 95
art: door
tags: mystery hollowstar danger
thread: hs_night
# v2: the seal's odds add up the whole plot and the whole Night (one check, a step per threshold of hs_seal). Each
# outcome closes the arc and is told in its own aftermath card (which belongs to no arc, so it still comes).
scene: A vast domed cavern under the lake, a round door of black stone standing open a crack, and through it a star that is pure absence.
text: Beyond the wall, the round door, open a crack, and through the crack the Hollow Star looks at you. It is beautiful, and it is hungry, and it speaks in your own voice: "You came all this way. Open me. Or take what I'm offering. Or run." {flag(night_kael): Kael is beside you, frost spreading from his feet.|{flag(night_ilse): Ilse is beside you, breathing steady for once.|{flag(night_maud): Maud is beside you{has_item(edmunds_silver_wand): , and Edmund's wand in your hand is humming the bell's note|, humming the bell's note under her breath}.|{flag(night_isolde): The headmistress stands beside you, her ring lit like a lamp.|You are alone.}}}}
> seal: Seal the door
  hint: Needs the star key, the founders' secret or a ward-ring. Arcana; everything you did tonight counts. It can fail.
  when: flag(star_key) or flag(knows_founders_seal) or clue(knows_founders_seal) or flag(warden_trial) or flag(gave_star_key)
  alignment +small
  hs_prep = clue(seven_locks) + clue(star_key) + clue(ilse_truth) + (rel(kael) >= 18) + (rel(ilse) >= 18) + (rel(maud) >= 18) + (rel(isolde) >= 18) + 2 * (flag(sided_wardens) or flag(sided_dumonts)) + flag(sided_self) + (alignment >= 30) + (alignment >= 60) + (spell_level(starlight) >= 1) + (spell_level(ward) >= 1) + flag(wardens_noticed)
  hs_seal = hs_prep + 2 * flag(hs_tunnel_clear) + 2 * flag(hs_threshold_read) + 2 * flag(cult_broken) + 2 * flag(shadow_beaten) + 2 * (flag(star_key) or flag(gave_star_key)) + 2 * flag(night_isolde) + flag(night_maud) - night_hurt
  challenge spell master slim +1 if hs_seal >= 4 +1 if hs_seal >= 8 +1 if hs_seal >= 12 +1 if hs_seal >= 16:
    win:
      flag hollow_sealed
      close hollowstar
      renown +huge
      mood +large
      lose star_mark
      lose hollow_dreams
      if flag(night_kael) or (met(kael) and rel(kael) >= 0 and not flag(night_ilse) and not flag(night_maud) and not flag(night_isolde)):
        queue hs_aftermath in 1
      else:
        queue hs_aftermath_quiet in 1
      say: {flag(star_key): The star key turns in the round door, and you|{flag(gave_star_key) and flag(night_isolde): The headmistress turns the star key in the round door, and you|You}} speak the founders' words with everything you have, and the door grinds shut. The Star screams without sound. Above you, the ice cracks from shore to shore, and the lake breathes again.
    lose:
      flag hollow_failed
      close hollowstar
      lose hollow_dreams
      queue hs_aftermath_lost in 1
      if flag(night_kael):
        rel kael +large
        say: Your seal falters. Kael throws every ounce of frost in him into it, and it still isn't enough: the door stays ajar. The last thing you see is the headmistress's lantern coming down the tunnel.
      else:
        say: Your seal falters and breaks, and takes most of you with it. The door stays ajar. The last thing you see is the headmistress's lantern coming down the tunnel.
> bargain: Accept the Star's bargain
  hint: Its power, now, and a voice in your head forever. Only for those it has already tempted.
  when: alignment <= -30 or flag(hollow_tempted)
  flag hollow_bargain
  close hollowstar
  alignment -large
  gold +huge
  mana +large
  learn_spell eclipse
  if not has(star_mark):
    gain star_mark
  gain star_crowned
  lose hollow_dreams
  queue hs_aftermath_bargain in 1
  if alignment <= -30:
    mood +medium
    say: You take what it offers, and it feels like coming home. The door closes on its own, for now. The Star settles into the back of your mind like a cat finding a warm lap, and pours itself into your hands.
  else:
    mood -large
    say: You take what it offers. The door closes on its own, for now. The Star settles into the back of your mind like a cat finding a warm lap, and pours itself into your hands, and you can't stop shaking.
> open: Open the door
  hint: It wants out. Only one already deep in the Hollow could walk through beside it.
  when: alignment <= -60 or flag(hollow_tempted)
  if alignment <= -60:
    flag hollow_freed
    close hollowstar
    alignment -large
    arcana +large
    gain star_mark
    lose hollow_dreams
    renown -medium
    queue hs_aftermath_freed in 1
    say: You set your palm on the black stone and push. The door swings wide. The Star rises past you like a breath held for three hundred years, and on its way out it touches your shoulder, the way a lord touches a sword. Above, every candle in Lumenhold goes out at once.
  else:
    end ending_hollow_claimed
> flee: Run
  close hollowstar
  mood -large
  flag hollow_fled
  queue hs_aftermath_fled in 1
  say: You run. You run until the tunnel spits you out onto the shore, and you don't look back once. Behind you, under the ice, the door is still ajar.

@event hs_aftermath
title: After the Thaw
class: story
tone: eerie
trigger: queued
art: sun
tags: hollowstar story
# No arc (v2): it comes after the arc is closed.
scene: The lake glittering in spring sunshine, students skimming stones, a bandaged figure sitting on the jetty.
on_show:
  close hollowstar
  if night_hurt >= 2:
    health -medium
  elif night_hurt >= 1:
    health -small
text: The lake glitters as if nothing happened. Most of the academy believes there was a strange spring frost. The headmistress knows better. So does Kael, who finds you on the jetty with two cups of tea. {flag(ilse_taken): He doesn't say his sister's name. She went north before dawn, with the man in grey.|{flag(dumont_reunited) and not flag(ilse_went_north): Ilse is further down the jetty, pretending not to watch.|}}
> left: Sit with him in silence
  rel kael +large
  mood +medium
  say: You watch the water. It's just water, now. Kael's tea, for once, doesn't freeze.
> right: Tell him how you feel
  if spark(kael) >= 25 and rel(kael) >= 0:
    spark kael +large
    bond kael partner
    say: He kisses you, and for the first time since you've known him, his hands are warm.
  else:
    rel kael +large
    if bond(kael) == "none":
      bond kael close
    say: "I owe you everything," he says. "I'm not good at owing people. I'll learn."

@event hs_aftermath_lost
title: The Headmistress Closed It
class: story
tone: grim
trigger: queued
actor: isolde
art: door
tags: hollowstar story
# No arc (v2): it comes after the arc is closed. The seal's cost is paid here.
scene: An infirmary bed by a window, the lake thawed outside, a tall woman with newly white hair sitting beside it without her silver ring.
on_show:
  close hollowstar
  health -large
text: You wake in the infirmary. The lake has thawed, and the door is shut: the headmistress came down after you and closed it with her own hands. She is sitting by your bed. Her hair has gone white overnight, and her silver ring is gone. {flag(ilse_taken): Ilse went north before dawn.|}
> left: "I'm sorry."
  meet isolde
  rel isolde +medium
  mood -medium
  say: "You went down," she says. "Most don't. The door is shut, and I am old, and that was always the price for someone." She pats your hand once, like a chess move. You can't stop thinking about it for weeks.
> right: "What did it cost you?"
  meet isolde
  lore +small
  mood -large
  say: She tells you, plainly, and you wish she hadn't. The seal will hold for another lifetime. She won't. She asks you not to tell the others, and you don't, and it weighs on you.

@event hs_kael_sister
title: The Sister
class: story
tone: eerie
when: flag(kael_ally) and turn >= 22 and not flag(met_sister) and not flag(ilse_in_village) and not met(ilse)
weight: 10
art: snow
tags: mystery hollowstar
thread: hs_investigation
scene: A girl in white furs standing at the academy gates in a snowstorm that is falling only on her.
text: A girl in white furs is waiting at the gates in a private snowstorm. Kael's younger sister, Ilse. "If my brother won't open it," she says, "I will. Unless you can give me a reason not to."
> left: Convince her
  flag met_sister
  find lead_white_furs
  find ilse_truth
  hs_investigation_progress
  challenge negotiate journeyman:
    win:
      rel kael +large
      say: You talk for an hour. Then she's crying, and Kael is holding her, and the snow stops. She stays in the village to be near him.
    lose:
      mood -small
      say: She listens politely and leaves. "We'll see each other again," she says. "Beneath the water."
> right: Warn the headmistress
  flag met_sister
  find lead_white_furs
  find ilse_truth
  rel isolde +small
  hs_investigation_progress
  rel kael -small
  say: Ilse is escorted from the grounds. Kael understands. He says he understands. He's quiet for a long time.
